From: Gee <gehee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtl8xxxu: keep the AP's group key slot when a station leaves

In AP mode the vif's hw_key_idx holds the group key's CAM slot (set_key
records it for the group key only), and broadcast/multicast frames are
sent with it. DISABLE_KEY reset it for every key, so a station leaving -
its pairwise key removed - left the AP sending broadcast and multicast
without the group key: DHCP offers and ARP requests no longer reached the
stations still associated or joining after (an iPhone stayed on a
169.254.x address). Reset it only when the group key itself goes.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
@@ -7076,7 +7076,15 @@
 		val32 = CAM_CMD_POLLING | CAM_CMD_WRITE |
 			key->hw_key_idx << CAM_CMD_KEY_SHIFT;
 		rtl8xxxu_write32(priv, REG_CAM_CMD, val32);
-		rtlvif->hw_key_idx = 0xff;
+		/*
+		 * hw_key_idx of the vif is the group key's slot (set for the
+		 * group key only, above): a station leaving, its pairwise key
+		 * removed, must not reset it, or broadcast and multicast go out
+		 * without the group key and DHCP offers and ARP no longer reach
+		 * the stations still there or joining after.
+		 */
+		if (!(key->flags & IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE))
+			rtlvif->hw_key_idx = 0xff;
 		clear_bit(key->hw_key_idx, priv->cam_map);
 		retval = 0;
 		break;
